{"id": "cf501882-f287-4f78-ae39-95a822271970", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:55:37.399508", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "7a584d7c-cfed-409c-969c-a6ef560e6058", "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-1e28d508-221a-44a2-9202-6ce181f1ae05", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Handoff recorded; waiting for researcher review."}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "7a584d7c-cfed-409c-969c-a6ef560e6058", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 19}
{"id": "4ef7857d-eced-42d9-8d55-a92172af8871", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:55:54.192578", "source": "user", "parent_id": "cf501882-f287-4f78-ae39-95a822271970", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Good inspection work and a clean experimental skeleton. Before I authorize the main work, here are the resolutions to your four open questions — these are explicit assumptions I am making as the researcher, not source-confirmed facts, so please restate them verbatim in the final design's Assumptions section so a reader can audit them. (a) Scope both TorchOpt Adam entry points individually in the design: `torchopt.Adam` as the standard fused optimizer and `torchopt.MetaAdam` (or whichever current alias wraps the differentiable / fused-meta variant TorchOpt ships) as a second condition. The reason is that 'fusing operations within Adam' can mean either fused-state fused-step kernels (plain Adam) or fused-meta-differentiable stepping (MetaAdam); both are fair readings and the design should not silently pick one. (b) Fix the TorchViz call to `torchviz.make_dot(loss, params=dict(model.named_parameters()))` in both conditions so the rendered graph covers the autograd edges into every leaf parameter; this is the slice where the optimizer-step subgraph actually attaches, and it matches the question's 'gradient graph' wording. (c) Interpret 'gradient graph' as the full autograd graph visible to `make_dot` under (b), i.e. forward + backward edges terminating at parameter leaves. Treat the optimizer-step subgraph (param.grad consumption → next param.data write) as the primary slicing region for the fused-vs-unfused claim, and forward/backward portions as secondary. Promote optimizer-subgraph node count and operator diversity to primary metrics; full-graph node/edge count, depth, and cyclomatic complexity become secondary. (d) Mirror TorchOpt's actual codepath as the primary C1 implementation, and additionally include a third condition C_ped (C-pedagogical): an explicit unfused re-implementation of the Adam update in plain PyTorch ops, used as a sanity reference so the comparison is not 'whatever PyTorch's Adam emits' vs 'TorchOpt'. This makes the interpretability claim testable without conflating framework defaults with the conceptual unfused baseline. Other guidance: keep the per-block partition you proposed (moment-1, moment-2, bias correction, param update, weight decay); require ≥5 paired seeds; report matched-pairs sign test plus matched-pairs rank-biserial effect size; lock device to CPU and dtype to float32; forbid any package install in the protocol (design-only). Approaching now — produce the final experiment design with rationale, controls, full operationalized metric definitions (so a future executor could implement them mechanically), the analysis plan, the assumption list, and a feasibility note about the bubblewrap environment. Do not claim any experiment was run. Do not fabricate TorchOpt or TorchViz internals beyond what is needed to specify the API surface; if a detail cannot be stated confidently from general knowledge of these libraries, label it as a protocol-level placeholder to be confirmed at execution time.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 20}
