, and forward/backward portions as secondary. Promote optimizer-subgraph node count and operator diversity to primary metrics; full-graph node/edge count, depth, and cyclomatic complexity become secondary.\\\"\\n   (d) \\\"Mirror TorchOpt's actual codepath as the primary C1 implementation, and additionally include a third condition C_ped (C-pedagogical): an explicit unfused re-implementation of the Adam update in plain PyTorch ops, used as a sanity reference so the comparison is not 'whatever PyTorch's Adam emits' vs 'TorchOpt'. This makes the interpretability claim testable without conflating framework defaults with the conceptual unfused baseline.\\\"\\n   These are researcher-provided assumptions, explicitly flagged as not source-confirmed, included verbatim for audit.\\n\\n11. Other design assumptions (non-verbatim, D.1..D.6).\\n   - D.1 The four conditions are the complete scope; no other Adam-fused variant (Apex, functorch torch.compile Adam) is in scope.\\n   - D.2 weight_decay=0.0 is locked to remove a B5 confound; a design choice, not a library default.\\n   - D.3 Op labels from make_dot are stable enough across conditions for the per-block bucketing in 5.4; if not, [P-7] default applies.\\n   - D.4 At least 5 paired seeds; 10 recommended. Sign test + rank-biserial are appropriate at this N.\\n   - D.5 CPU-only scope. Results not generalized to GPU-fused backends.\\n   - D.6 Design-only deliverable; no execution claimed. Specifies procedures a future executor could implement mechanically.\\n\\n12. Protocol placeholders to be confirmed at execution time.\\n   [P-1] Current TorchOpt alias for MetaAdam (e.g., torchopt.MetaAdam or torchopt.optim.meta.MetaAdam).\\n   [P-2] Supported kwarg set of torchviz.make_dot in the executor's installed version; canonical call is torchviz.make_dot(loss, params=dict(model.named_parameters())).\\n   [P-3] Parser choice for node/edge extraction (e.g., pydot from dot.source()).\\n   [P-4] Op-type label definition if make_dot strips op attributes under chosen kwargs; default rule documented in 5.1.\\n   [P-5] Eligibility rule when the immediate-successor heuristic fails; default is to exclude the run.\\n   [P-6] String-match rules for AccumulateGrad and param.grad consumer identification.\\n   [P-7] Default bucketing for ambiguous per-block nodes; cheapest-fit and flagged.\\n   [P-8] Final seed count; minimum 5, recommended 10.\\n\\nEnd of design. Awaiting reviewer feedback on metric definitions, controls, placeholders, or the qualitative walkthrough table format before any execution attempt.\",\"evidence\":\"(1) Workspace inspection: `ls -laR /workspace` returns a single 0600 file `task.json` (466 B); no other files exist, including no `track.md`. The only reference to `track.md` is the string \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" inside `task.json.documents`. (2) TorchOpt/TorchViz/torch: `find` up to depth 7 returned zero directory matches; Python 3.12.3 + pip 24.0 present but `import torch`, `import torchviz`, `import torchopt` all fail with `ModuleNotFoundError`; no install attempted. (3) Researcher resolutions (a)–(d) restated verbatim in Section 10 per explicit instruction to make them auditable. (4) No TorchOpt/TorchViz internals fabricated beyond the API surface needed to specify the entry points; every detail that cannot be stated confidently is labeled with protocol placeholders [P-1]..[P-8]. (5) No execution claimed; design specifies procedures at a level a future executor could implement mechanically. (6) Format note: previous turns in this session had a serialization issue when array items contained nested XML-looking fragments; this submission encodes `assumptions` and `uncertainties` as flat single-line items to avoid that issue.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Researcher assumptions (a) through (d) recorded verbatim in Section 10 are taken as explicit assumptions of this design.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"D.1 Four conditions (C0=torch.optim.Adam, C1=torchopt.Adam, C2=torchopt.MetaAdam, C_ped=unfused re-implementation) are the complete scope; no other fused-Adam variant in scope.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"D.2 weight_decay=0.0 locked across all conditions to control B5 reporting.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"D.3 make_dot op labels assumed stable enough across conditions for per-block bucketing; ambiguity handled by [P-7].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"D.4 At least 5 paired seeds (10 recommended); statistical claims limited to matched-pairs sign test and matched-pairs rank-biserial effect size.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"D.5 CPU-only scope; results not generalized to GPU-fused backends.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"D.6 Design-only deliverable; no execution claimed. Protocol placeholders [P-1] through [P-8] flagged for executor-time confirmation.</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"...</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"Current TorchOpt alias for the differentiable fused-meta Adam entry point [P-1].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Exact supported kwarg set of torchviz.make_dot in the executor's installed version [P-2], and whether params= triggers leaf-parameter edge rendering.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Parser used to extract node/edge counts from the rendered dot [P-3].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether op-type labels survive make_dot under the locked kwarg shape [P-4].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Heuristic for identifying the 'param + update' successor when multiple immediate successors of a parameter leaf exist [P-5].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"String-match rules for AccumulateGrad and param.grad consumer identification in the rendered graph [P-6].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Per-block bucketing default-overlap behavior when a node matches multiple blocks [P-7].</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Final seed count within the 5-10 recommended band [P-8].</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-72907640-6c68-